<Page title="Privacy policy" kicker="Legal" description="How personal data is handled on Grand Tour: cookie-free visit statistics, hosting logs and emails you send us." citations={['https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy', 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj']} lede="Grand Tour is built to need very little personal data. There are no accounts, no comments, no advertising trackers and no cookies.">
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The controller of personal data processed through grandtour.tourground.com is Tourground, the publisher of Grand Tour. Contact details are at the end of this page.</p>
  <h2>What we process, why, and on what basis</h2>
  <h3>1. Visit statistics</h3>
  <p>We count page views with Vercel Web Analytics. According to <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" rel="nofollow noopener">Vercel’s documentation</a>, it does not use cookies, identifies visitors by a hash created from the incoming request that is discarded after 24 hours, and reports only aggregated data such as the page, referrer, approximate location, device type, operating system and browser. We use it only to see which stories are read. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in running and improving the site (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR and UK GDPR).</p>
  <h3>2. Server logs</h3>
  <p>Our host, Vercel, processes technical request data (such as IP address, time, requested address and browser details) to deliver pages and protect the service from abuse. Legal basis: legitimate interest in operating a secure website.</p>
  <h3>3. Newsletter and emails you send us</h3>
  <p>If you email us to subscribe to the newsletter, we use your email address only to send you new-story emails, until you ask us to stop (legal basis: your consent, Article 6(1)(a); you can withdraw it at any time by replying “Unsubscribe”). If you email us for any other reason, we use your message to reply (legal basis: legitimate interest in answering you).</p>
  <p>We do not sell personal data, share it for advertising, or use it for automated decision-making.</p>
  <h2>Who receives it</h2>
  <p>Vercel Inc. (hosting and analytics) and our email provider, acting as our processors. Vercel is based in the United States; where data is transferred outside the UK or EU, it is protected by the safeguards the law requires, such as standard contractual clauses.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Analytics data is aggregated as described above. Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Other emails are kept only as long as needed to deal with them.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask for access to, correction of or deletion of your personal data, object to processing based on legitimate interest, and withdraw consent at any time. You can also complain to your data-protection authority, such as the UK Information Commissioner’s Office or the CNIL in France.</p>
  <h2>Sites we link to</h2>
  <p>Operator websites, the Tourground directory and our sources have their own privacy policies, which apply when you visit them.</p>
</Page>
